.ad
.fi

.SH ARGUMENTS
.nf
.na
None
.ad
.fi

.SH DESCRIPTION

The
.B auto-add-hosts-entry
command adds an entry to /etc/hosts for the primary network interface.
Many systems by default only have an /etc/hosts entry for
"localhost", 127.0.0.1.  An entry containing the hostname and
IP address is necessary for many programs, such as web servers,
to function properly.

.SH RETURN VALUES

0 on success, non-zero error codes otherwise.

